#### Shared procedures used by every phase

Use the Bash tool (Git Bash). Shell state does not persist between Bash calls, so every block starts with `source <SCRATCH>/env.sh`. `<SCRATCH>` is your session scratchpad in POSIX form, e.g. `cygpath -u 'C:\Users\...\scratchpad'`.

**S0: `<SCRATCH>/env.sh`.** Create this in Phase 0. If a later phase runs in a new session, recreate it and restore the baseline (see Phase 0, step 6).

```bash
# <SCRATCH>/env.sh - source at the top of every Bash block
export SCRATCH="/c/Users/.../scratchpad"      # this session's scratchpad, POSIX form
export REPO=/d/projects/mcp-task-manager
export B="$SCRATCH/baseline"
export FLAKY='^(TestBoardShowsBranchChip|TestCopyButtonHasNoHtmxAttributes)$'
export RACE_TASK_RUN='Phase|BoardSnapshot|Detail|BlockedMap|TestServiceRace|TestServiceNoSelfDeadlock'
export RACE_WEB_SKIP='^(TestEscaping|TestBoardShowsBranchChip|TestCopyButtonHasNoHtmxAttributes)$'
cd "$REPO" || return 1

# -h matters: with several files grep would prefix file names and break the match
failnames() { grep -hE '^[[:space:]]*--- FAIL: ' "$@" | sed -E 's/^[[:space:]]*--- FAIL: ([^ ]+).*/\1/' | sort -u; }

# gate <label>: build, full suite with no new failures vs baseline, no package that
# fails to compile, storage still ok, targeted race runs green, no data race.
gate() {
  local A="$B/after-$1"; mkdir -p "$A"
  go build ./... || { echo "GATE FAIL: go build"; return 1; }
  go test -count=1 ./... > "$A/full.txt" 2>&1
  if grep -E '\[(build|setup) failed\]' "$A/full.txt"; then echo "GATE FAIL: a package does not compile"; return 1; fi
  failnames "$A/full.txt" > "$A/fails.txt"
  grep -vxF -f "$B/fails.txt" "$A/fails.txt" | grep -vE "$FLAKY" > "$A/new-fails.txt" || true
  if [ -s "$A/new-fails.txt" ]; then echo "GATE FAIL: new failures:"; cat "$A/new-fails.txt"; return 1; fi
  grep -qE '^ok[[:space:]]+github.com/gpayer/mcp-task-manager/internal/storage' "$A/full.txt" || { echo "GATE FAIL: internal/storage is not ok"; return 1; }
  go test -count=1 -race -run "$RACE_TASK_RUN" ./internal/task/ > "$A/race-task.txt" 2>&1 || { echo "GATE FAIL: task race run"; tail -30 "$A/race-task.txt"; return 1; }
  go test -count=1 -race -skip "$RACE_WEB_SKIP" ./internal/web/ > "$A/race-web.txt" 2>&1 || { echo "GATE FAIL: web race run"; tail -30 "$A/race-web.txt"; return 1; }
  if grep -l 'WARNING: DATA RACE' "$A"/race-*.txt; then echo "GATE FAIL: data race"; return 1; fi
  echo "GATE OK ($1)"
}

# CRLF-safe gofmt over the staged Go files (core.autocrlf=true makes plain `gofmt -l` list every file)
gofmt_staged() {
  local bad=0 f
  for f in $(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACM -- '*.go'); do
    if [ -n "$(tr -d '\r' < "$f" | gofmt -l)" ]; then echo "needs gofmt: $f"; bad=1; fi
  done
  [ "$bad" = 0 ] && echo "gofmt OK"
  return $bad
}
```

**S1: Baseline gate.** `gate <phase>` must print `GATE OK`. Every test name that fails after a change must already be in `$B/fails.txt` or be one of the two known flaky tests. Every new test must pass in the targeted runs. The full `go test ./...` cannot pass on this machine (F5, F6).

**S2: Formatting.** Run `gofmt_staged` after staging. If it names a file, run `gofmt -w <file>` (LF output is fine; git normalizes), re-stage, and re-run.

**S3: CSS clean-tree build (`<SCRATCH>/css-clean-build.sh`).** Create this in Phase 2. It is never put in the repo. It runs the repo's `scripts/build-css.sh` over exactly the **staged** tree. Untracked task artifacts (this task's research, design and plan) and unstaged edits, such as the user's modified `tasks/git-branch-per-task/git-branch-per-task.md`, never reach the scanner.

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# css-clean-build.sh check|apply
#   check: a build of the staged tree must equal the staged app.css
#   apply: copy the build into the working tree; print the rule diff vs the staged app.css
set -euo pipefail
REPO="${REPO:-/d/projects/mcp-task-manager}"
HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
EXP="$HERE/css-export"
BIN_NAME="tailwindcss-windows-x64-v4.3.3.exe"
CSS="internal/web/static/app.css"

rm -rf "$EXP"
git -C "$REPO" checkout-index -a -f --prefix="$(cygpath -m "$EXP")/"
mkdir -p "$EXP/.cache" "$REPO/.cache"
if [ -f "$REPO/.cache/$BIN_NAME" ]; then cp "$REPO/.cache/$BIN_NAME" "$EXP/.cache/"; fi
(cd "$EXP" && bash scripts/build-css.sh)            # downloads into $EXP/.cache on first use
if [ ! -f "$REPO/.cache/$BIN_NAME" ]; then cp "$EXP/.cache/$BIN_NAME" "$REPO/.cache/"; fi   # .cache/ is gitignored

rules() { tr '}' '\n'; }
case "${1:-check}" in
  check)
    if cmp -s "$EXP/$CSS" <(git -C "$REPO" show ":$CSS"); then
      echo "CSS CHECK OK: the staged app.css is what build-css.sh produces"
    else
      echo "CSS CHECK FAILED: rule diff (staged -> rebuilt):"
      diff <(git -C "$REPO" show ":$CSS" | rules) <(rules < "$EXP/$CSS") || true
      exit 1
    fi ;;
  apply)
    cp "$EXP/$CSS" "$REPO/$CSS"
    echo "app.css rule diff vs the staged app.css:"
    diff <(git -C "$REPO" show ":$CSS" | rules) <(rules < "$REPO/$CSS") || true ;;
  *) echo "usage: $0 check|apply" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
```

