### Cross-Phase Risks

#### Cross-cutting

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Tailwind auto source detection reads the working tree (F1) | `app.css` depends on untracked files and prose; the design's literal determinism check fails here | Always build via S3 (staged-tree export); exact expected diffs for P4/P5; S5 wording rule; post-phase `check` |
| Stray utilities from words in Go, test or doc text (F4) | Noise in the generated diff; a future clean rebuild is not a no-op | S5: avoid `@container` and bare `container`; the CSS test uses verified non-leaking strings; any unexpected rule blocks the phase until reworded |
| `go test ./...` cannot be green on Windows (F5, F6) | The acceptance criterion is only partially verifiable here | S1 subset gate plus targeted race runs (OQ5); report that a full run needs Linux/macOS; no WSL/Docker/CI test job exists |
| Flaky branch-chip tests, also under `-race` | False alarms, or masked regressions in branch-chip rendering | Excluded from the gate by exact name; informational `-count=5` run in P5; S6 manual copy-button check |
| CRLF working copy (`core.autocrlf=true`, no `.gitattributes`) | `gofmt -l` false positives; mixed endings after edits | `gofmt_staged` strips `\r`; git normalizes on add; Git Bash runs the CRLF script (verified) |
| Unrelated user changes in the tree | Accidentally committing the user's `tasks/` edit or task artifacts | S4 explicit-path staging; `git diff --cached --stat` before every commit; `checkout-index` exports exclude them |
| Stale immutable `app.css` in open browsers | Lanes look unstaggered after an upgrade | Documented hard reload (P6); fresh port in S6; follow-up cache-busting task (OQ4) |
| Lock-held directory listing per in-progress task per poll | Slightly longer `BoardSnapshot` under the mutex | Bounded by the in-progress count (design estimate: a few ms per poll per tab); `TestServiceRace` and the HTTP race test cover concurrency |
| Session change between phases | Lost scratch files and helper | Recreate `env.sh` and `css-clean-build.sh` from this plan; restore the baseline from the `test-baseline` task file; the Tailwind binary persists in `$REPO/.cache/` |

